<title>CHINA: Three Shanghai firms fined over Marlboro lighters.</title>
<headline>Three Shanghai firms fined over Marlboro lighters.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Shanghai firms have been ordered to pay Philip Morris Cos Inc 600,000 yuan in compensation for making and exporting 577,000 fake Marlboro cigarette lighters, the Wen Hui Bao daily said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The firms, Shanghai Lighter Factory, Shanghai Aviation Export &amp; Import Co and Shanghai Huanlong Craft Factory were also fined 50,000 yuan, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The case has been under investigation since October 1995, the newspaper added but gave no more details.</p>
</text>
